<title>USA: Viad cruise subsidiary to sell ship.</title>
<headline>Viad cruise subsidiary to sell ship.</headline>
<dateline>PORT CANAVERAL, Fla. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Viad Corp said Thursday its cruise subsidiary had agreed to sell one of its ships to Westrai Holdings Inc for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The company said Premier Cruise Lines will sell the S.S. Atlantic to Westrai's subsidiary Mediterranean Shipping Cruises, which is planning to sail the ship out of Genoa on June 1, it said.</p>
<p>The Atlantic, originally built in 1982, has a gross tonnage of 35,143 tons and has a passenger capacity of 1,550, it said.</p>
</text>
